{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הנה אנכי יצאתי לשטן", :translit "hineh anokhi yatzati lisatan", :gloss "Behold, I have gone forth as an adversary"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay on 'yatzati' (went forth) read as departing from one's characteristic attribute."}], :frame {:text "The verse's phrase 'I have gone forth as an adversary' is read as the angel declaring he departed from his customary attribute of mercy to take on an adversarial role. The concept of divine 'attributes' (middot) such as the attribute of mercy is drawn from rabbinic theology of God's governance through named middot, as developed in sources like Exodus Rabbah and applied to angelic function in midrashic literature.", :sources ["Exodus Rabbah 15:6"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay on 'yatzati' (went forth) read as departing from one's characteristic attribute.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:30:50.707483422Z", :model "glm-5.2"}